8	      "note": "The reduced boundary of the smooth DM stack Mbar_{6,6} is a simple normal crossings divisor. Etale-locally the miniversal base is a smooth complete local ring with independent node-smoothing parameters t_e and reduced equation product_e t_e=0; the normalization is the disjoint union of the smooth branches t_e=0, which is the choice of a distinguished node and descends under etale base change and under residual automorphisms that permute nodes. The resulting DM stack N is normal and finite birational onto the reduced boundary, hence is the normalization. The one-line Ext^2 vanishing is the standard Deligne-Mumford local description rather than a self-contained cotangent-complex computation, but the descended identification is the classical clutching/normalization of the boundary.",
