23	      "note": "For finite G acting on a complex DM stack Y, Cartan-Leray plus averaging over Q gives H^*([Y/G];Q)=H^*(Y;Q)^G; invariants and coinvariants agree over Q. SRC-0003 defines det E(Gamma) as the determinant of the Aut(Gamma)-permutation representation on the set of edges, and writes the first arrow of the weight complex (pullback to the normalization of the boundary, |E|=1) as oplus H^k(Mbar_Gamma)^{Aut} with no extra local system; det E appears in the |E|=2 term. Every graph here has one edge, so Aut fixes that unique edge, det E is the trivial representation, and (H^*(Mbar_Gamma) tensor det E)^{Aut}=H^*(Mbar_Gamma)^{Aut}=H^*([Mbar_Gamma/Aut]). In particular the loop S_2 acts geometrically by swapping the two branch markings of Mbar_{5,8} and trivially on the singleton edge set, so the contribution is ordinary S_2-invariants, which is exactly H^* of the quotient in clause (i). SRC-0002 (8.1) uses the same one-edge-without-det / two-edge-with-det split. The theorem names this source and asserts no Tate type, Gysin twist, or image statement; none is used.",
