{12}\\\\) / \\\\(S[12]\\\\)\\nNONE FOUND.\\n\\n### Compact \\\\(\\\\overline{\\\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}\\\\) cohomology statements (degree / \\\\((g,n)\\\\) as written)\\n- L6: `This theorem does not re-prove the open residual W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), and does not by itself conclude H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) cong Q(-8)^{oplus b_16}.`\\n- L17: `Check that the boundary of Mbar_{5,8} is outside RED-0001, assemble compact H^{16}(Mbar_{5,8}) by THM-0003, and conclude that the (6,6) boundary-image is Tate.`\\n- L24: `Type the separating Kunneth terms of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6}).`\\n- L25: `Assemble compact H^{16}(Mbar_{5,8}) from its open residual.`\\n- L35 (`FND-0031`): `Hence only the m=0 term H^{2d-16}(Mbar_{g,n}) and the single d_1 Gysin map from the codimension-one strata H^{2d-18}(D^{(1)})(-1) can contribute; [...] they express the open input in terms of the still-unknown H^{16}(Mbar_{g,n}).`\\n- L44 (`FND-0048`): `For M_{6,6}, the pure piece W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)=im(H^{26}(\\\\overline M_{6,6};Q)->H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)) is not identified by any supplied argument with a codimension-13 decorated stable-graph complex generated by algebraic cotangent and gluing classes; treating that image as a subquotient of such a complex is circular and does not rule out surviving non-Tate pure weight-26 summands.`\\n- L61 (`FND-0071`): `A low-degree diagonal statement that, at 2r=2g+n-2, only the kernel of restriction H^{2r}(\\\\overline{M}_{g,n})\\u2192H^{2r}(D) is Tate does not by itself make the whole group H^{2r}(\\\\overline{M}_{g,n}) Tate; boundary-supported classes and the full stratified contribution must still be controlled.`\\n- L62 (`FND-0072`): `No complete unconditional proof that H^{16}(\\\\overline{M}_{6,6};Q) is a direct sum of Q(-8) is supplied by ATT-0027; graph-complex/arc-contraction slogans without Aut-invariants, Gysin shifts, differentials, and higher-genus primitives do not discharge this.`\\n- L71 (`FND-0089` metadata): `'applies_to': 'attempts proving low-degree bound