e exactly 0, which is the unique value making the failure condition a single Abel-Jacobi condition O_C(\\u0393) \\u2245 L rather than a positive-degree Brill-Noether condition (n \\u2265 7). The identification proved for (6,6) is therefore structurally specific to the borderline degree and does not transport to neighbouring n by the same argument.`\\n- L84 (`FND-0105`): `The residual twist is then forced away by degree: SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 records deg(O_{P(E^vee)}(2)|_C) = 2(2g-2+4*2), i.e. deg(O_{P(E^vee)}(1)|_C) = 2g+6 = deg(omega_C tensor gamma^*O(2)), and a twist by gamma^*A shifts this by 4 deg A, so deg A = 0 and A ~= O_{P^1}. Hence W_5 ~= omega_C^2(-D), equivalently L ~= omega_C(-D) and M ~= O_C(D).`\\n- L114 (`FND-0156`): `PACKET/CE CONVENTION (SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6, with the dual sign required by W:=O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*F^vee and by the degree line of that lemma, not by the lemma's one-line 'set W_{f_i}=O(2) tensor gamma^*O(f_i)' which omits the minus): W_f=(O_X(2) tensor gamma^*O_{P^1}(-f))|_C for f=4,5, filtered as 0->W_4->W->W_5->0 with deg W_4=20 and deg W_5=16.`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (2) Published cohomology of \\\\(\\\\overline{\\\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}\\\\)\\n\\n### \\u201ctautological range\\u201d\\nNONE FOUND.\\n\\n### \\u201cpublished even cohomology through degree 14\\u201d\\n- L15: `Discharge every separating H^{16} Kunneth term from published even cohomology through degree 14 and CKgP/induction on non-residual factors.`\\n\\n### Odd-degree vanishing \\\\(H^1,H^3,H^5,H^7,H^9,H^{11},H^{13},H^{15}\\\\) of \\\\(\\\\overline{\\\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}\\\\)\\nNONE FOUND.\\n\\n(The only nearby \\\\(H^{15}\\\\) wording is not vanishing of odd cohomology of \\\\(\\\\overline{\\\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}\\\\): L126 `D proper, so H^{15}(D;Q) has weights <= 15` and L126 `properness of D (weights of H^{15}(D) are <= 15)`.)\\n\\n### \\\\(H^{11}\\\\) / cusp forms / weight-11 motive \\\\(LS_{12}\\\\) / \\\\(S[12]\\\\)\\nNONE FOUND.\\n\\n### Compact \\\\(\\\\overline{\\\\mat