 Findings / constraints: separating boundary, Kunneth, product of two \\\\(\\\\overline{\\\\mathcal{M}}\\\\)\\u2019s, degree 16 on a boundary component, Tate type of \\\\(H^k(\\\\overline{\\\\mathcal{M}}_{g,n})\\\\), C66BAR-SEP\\n\\n### Constraints\\n- L8: `## Canonical geometric bottleneck: Non-separating boundary divisor`\\n- L12: `Non-separating normalization: `[Mbar_{5,8}/S_2], where S_2 exchanges the two branches of the node; its ordered atlas Mbar_{5,8} is the unique RED-0001 residual pair in the boundary of Mbar_{6,6}`.`\\n- L13: `Separating type: `Quotients [Mbar_Gamma/Aut(Gamma)] for one-edge separating graphs, with ordered atlas Mbar_{g1,n1} x Mbar_{g2,n2}, g1+g2=6 and n1+n2=8; cohomology is taken with Aut(Gamma)-invariants and the determinant-edge convention`.`\\n- L14: `Identify every component of hat{partial} Mbar_{6,6} as [Mbar_Gamma/Aut(Gamma)], including [Mbar_{5,8}/S_2] for the non-separating graph, and retain the determinant-edge convention.`\\n- L15: `Discharge every separating H^{16} Kunneth term from published even cohomology through degree 14 and CKgP/induction on non-residual factors.`\\n- L17: `Check that the boundary of Mbar_{5,8} is outside RED-0001, assemble compact H^{16}(Mbar_{5,8}) by THM-0003, and conclude that the (6,6) boundary-image is Tate.`\\n- L24: ``C66BAR-SEP` (weakest-sufficient-proof): Type the separating Kunneth terms of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6}). Dependencies: C66BAR-GRAPH.`\\n- L25: ``C58-COMPACT` (weakest-sufficient-proof): Assemble compact H^{16}(Mbar_{5,8}) from its open residual. Dependencies: C58-OPEN, C58-BOUNDARY.`\\n- L26: ``C66BAR-IMAGE` (weakest-sufficient-proof): Conclude that the (6,6) boundary-image is Tate. Dependencies: C66BAR-GRAPH, C66BAR-SEP, C58-COMPACT.`\\n- L6: `The image of the boundary map H_{16}(hat{partial} Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H_{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) from the normalization of the boundary of the moduli stack of stable 6-pointed genus-6 curves is a finite direct sum of Q(8). Equivalently this image is a pure polarizable Tate Hodge structure of weight -16 and type Q(8). A disproof must exhibit a surviving non-Tate summand in this image. This theorem does not re-prove the open residual W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), and does not by itself conclude H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) cong Q(-8)^{oplus b_16}.`\\n- L10: `Boundary sequence: `THM-0003 / SRC-0002 Eq. (6.1): H_{16}(hat{partial} Mbar_{6,6}) -> H_{16}(Mbar_{6,6}) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6}) -> 0`.`\\n\\nNo FND line contains the string `C66BAR-SEP`.\\n\\n### `FND-0031` (L35)\\n`In the Deligne weight spectral sequence of (Mbar_{g,n}, boundary), the corner gr^W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n}) computing the RED-0001 open input sits at spectral-sequence depth m = weight - degree = 0. Hence only the m=0 term H^{2d-16}(Mbar_{g,n}) and the single d_1 Gysin map from the codimension-one strata H^{2d-18}(D^{(1)})(-1) can contribute; strata of codimension >= 2, multi-edge stable graphs, and higher differentials (E_2-degeneration) are all irrelevant to this corner. Dualizing, the resulting cokernel is identical to the boundary sequence of THM-0003, so the weight spectral sequence and the Getzler-Kapranov graph complex yield no information beyond THM-0003 at this corner and cannot break the circularity: they express the open input in terms of the still-unknown H^{16}(Mbar_{g,n}). Any attempt of this approach type must add an independent input for the m=0 term or attack a different corner.`\\n\\n### `FND-0034` (L38)\\n`For (g,n)=(6,6) the non-separating boundary divisor has normalization Mbar_{5,8}, not Mbar_{5,7} as ATT-0014 states: the genus drops by one and the normalization gains TWO legs at the node, 6+2=8, and dim Mbar_{5,8} = 3*5-3+8 = 20 = 21-1 confirms codimension one while dim Mbar_{5,7} = 19 does not. This matters beyond arithmetic: combined with the depth-one restriction above, the only Gysin source into H^{26}(Mbar_{6,6}) other than separating-divisor products is Mbar_{5,8}, and (5,8) is itself an unresolved pair in RED-0001. Any depth-one attack on (6,6) therefore couples directly to the (5,8) case rather than to strictly simpler discharged inputs, and the correct edge-decorated E_1 term is (H^*(Mbar_Gamma) tensor det E_Gamma)^{Aut(Gamma)} -- the determinant twist on the edge set, omitted by ATT-0014, kills contributions whose automorphisms permute edges oddly or swap the two branches of the non-separating node.`\\n\\n### `FND-0071` (L61)\\n`A low-degree diagonal statement that, at 2r=2g+n-2, only the kernel of restriction H^{2r}(\\\\overline{M}_{g,n})\\u2192H^{2r}(D) is Tate does not by itself make the whole group H^{2r}(\\\\overline{M}_{g,n}) Tate; boundary-supported classes and the full stratified contribution must still be controlled.`\\n\\n### `FND-0072` (L62)\\n`No complete unconditional proof that H^{16}(\\\\overline{M}_{6,6};Q) is a direct sum of Q(-8) is supplied by ATT-0027; graph-complex/arc-contraction slogans without Aut-invariants, Gysin shifts, differentials, and higher-genus primitives do not discharge this.`\\n\\n### `FND-0089` (L71)\\n`A purely combinatorial ordered-arc insertion operator does not supply a chain homotopy on the K\\u00fcnneth-decorated one-edge restriction complex: without a cohomological rule for how vertex classes transform under arc insertion, and without a comparison theorem identifying the arc complex with the restriction/\\u010cech complex for clutching maps, one cannot conclude that the simultaneous one-edge kernel P^m_{g,n} is Tate.`\\n\\n### `FND-0168` (L126)\\n`Scope: (g,n)=(6,6) over C with Q-coefficients; Mbar_{6,6} the smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack of dimension d=21, D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6} its proper boundary, Z the balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus. (1) K := ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q)) is canonically isomorphic, as a pure polarizable Hodge structure of weight 16, to Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q) -- the top weight graded piece of H^{16}_c and the entire degree-16 compact-support corner of M_{6,6} -- and is canonically the Hodge-structure dual of the RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), with Q(-8) dual to Q(8). This uses only smoothness of M_{6,6} (weights of H^{16}_c are <= 16), properness of D (weights of H^{15}(D) are <= 15) and strictness. It is a global invariant of M_{6,6} and carries no support condition. The separate Poincare identification W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) = W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21) (FND-0001) is a different map and must not be conflated with this duality. (2) For any pure Q-Hodge structure V of weight 16, 'V is a finite direct sum of Q(-8)' and 'V is spanned by its Hodge (8,8)-classes' are the same condition (V_C = V^{8,8}) by the definition of Hodge type; neither polarizability nor semisimplicity of the category of pure polarizable weight-16 Q-Hodge structures is needed for this equivalence, and neither adds information to it. Applied to K, the equivalence is a restatement of the target, not a reduction: it imposes no support condition and produces no cycle class. (Semisimplicity, per FND-0033, only excludes extension gaps at this corner.) (3) Give 'the contribution supported on Z' its only standard meaning by first fixing a closed support Y in M_{6,6} containing the image of Z. Since Gr^W is exact on mixed Hodge structures, the Borel-Moore localization sequence yields an exact sequence W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q). Consequently: (3a) if the Z-supported contribution means the image of the first map, then K Tate of type Q(-8) implies that contribution is Tate (a sub-object of a type-(8,8) structure is of type (8,8)), so Z-Tate is necessary; but the converse -- the direction the reduction needs -- does not follow, since it additionally requires a support-exhaustion input, namely vanishing or Tate-ness of the quotient injecting into W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16} of the complement of Y. No such input is established for (6,6). (3b) if it means W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) itself, then neither direction follows, since only the image of that group is constrained by K. ATT-0116 fixes neither reading. Hence the asserted equivalence 'the contribution supported on Z is Tate of the exact target type if and only if K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes' is unproved and is a non-sequitur in its load-bearing direction. This is a statement about a missing hypothesis, not a demonstration that the two sides have different truth values: if the RED-0001 target is Tate, both sides hold, so the biconditional cannot be refuted by exhibiting differing truth values. (4) 'K is spanned by algebraic fundamental classes of codimension-8 cycles of Mbar_{6,6} supported on a closure of Z' implies 'K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes', but the converse is the Hodge conjecture in codimension 8 on the 21-dimensional Mbar_{6,6}, which is unproved in general beyond the (1,1) case; writing 'equivalently' between the two silently assumes it. (5) Independently of (3) and (4), the support clause carries two further undischarged obligations: (5a) a closed (stratified) embedding of the balanced reduced-support model into M_{6,6}/Mbar_{6,6} together with a Gysin map -- that model is an open piece of the failure locus (FND-0052), and FND-0147 supplies only a representable unramified quasi-finite monomorphism to M_{6,6}, which is not a closed immersion of a pure-codimension-4 closed substack; (5b) the Gysin degree shift H^{8}(Z-tilde;Q)(-4) -> H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) for a 17-dimensional codimension-4 support with a suitable smooth model Z-tilde. The phrase 'codimension-8 cycles supported on the closure of Z' is itself degree-consistent (codimension 8 in Mbar_{6,6} equals codimension 4 on the 17-dimensional support), so the defect is the unwritten shift and the missing closed embedding, not the codimension label; the fundamental class of the support itself lies in H^{8}, not H^{16}. Not asserted: that K fails to be Tate; that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate; that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K; any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q); any claim for (g,n) other than (6,6), although the logical structure of (2)-(4) is general. Confirmed and untouched: ATT-0116 clause (a) and claims CL-01 through CL-04.`\\n\\n### `FND-0169` (L127)\\n`Over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] be the smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of pure dimension 15 of balanced genus-six degree-four covers (FND-0162). Let S range over reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family in the sense of FND-0167, including connected components of reduced separated finite-type etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal. The constant-coefficient corner Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) is not an invariant of the stack Hbar^bal: it depends on S. Explicitly, the mu_3-Kummer cover C->M_{0,4} cut out by y^3=x(x-1), with smooth projective model Cbar of genus one, yields a nonempty irreducible finite-etale cover Mtilde of M_{0,18} whose Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Mtilde;Q) contains a nonzero Hodge type (15,1), obtained as the compact-support Kunneth summand Q(-1) tensor H^{1,0}(Cbar)^{tensor 14} and surviving removal of the pairwise-diagonal locus of dimension at most 14 because Hodge numbers of compactly supported cohomology vanish in filtration degree strictly larger than dimension (Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)). By the Bujokas-Patel theorem that the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle F of a general cover in the classical simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g} is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (hence for (d,g)=(4,6)), together with FND-0159 (the classical Hurwitz space is etale over the configuration space of r=2g+2d-2=18 points), there is a connected finite-etale Hurwitz chart X over M_{0,18} whose balanced open is nonempty. Finite-etale pullback/trace of the type-(15,1) class along a connected component Xtilde of X times_{M_{0,18}} Mtilde, followed by compact-support localization onto the balanced open V of Xtilde (FND-0165), produces a connected smooth 15-fold V, etale over Hbar^bal, with Gr^{15,1} Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;C) nonzero. Thus Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8). For any allowed atlas U, the disjoint union U sqcup V is again an allowed atlas and compactly supported cohomology is additive, so the same non-Tate summand appears in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U sqcup V;Q). Consequently the j=8 instance of hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167, namely that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8), is false for some allowed S. FND-0167 itself does not assert (H-S). Any campaign statement that asserts or requires (H-S) while universally quantifying over a reduced locally Noetherian scheme atlas of Hbar^bal, or over all reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying the balanced setup, is therefore false as stated rather than merely unproved. (H-S) may be asserted only for a specifically named atlas, or replaced by a stack-level statement, which requires a compact-support mixed-Hodge formalism for Deligne-Mumford stacks that FND-0165 explicitly withholds. This does not address Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U): the FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into a sum of Tate twists of corners of S, so it cannot transport non-Tateness from S to Z, and the discriminant in the Abel-Jacobi P^2-bundle has dimension 16 so F^{15} H_c^{16} need not vanish there.`\\n\\n### `FND-0170` (L128)\\n`Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let d\\u22652 be an integer. Let B=M_{0,4}\\u2245P^1 minus {0,1,\\u221e}. Let Cbar be the smooth projective connected curve with function field C(x,y) and equation y^3=x(x-1): the degree-three map Cbar\\u2192P^1 given by x is totally ramified over exactly 0,1,\\u221e (valuations of x(x-1) equal 1,1,\\u22122, none divisible by 3), and Riemann-Hurwitz gives 2g(Cbar)\\u22122=3(\\u22122)+3(2)=0, so Cbar has genus one. Let C be Cbar minus those three ramification points, so C\\u2192B is connected finite etale of degree three. Compact-support localization yields Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q)\\u2245H^1(Cbar;Q) of Hodge types (1,0) and (0,1), and H_c^2(C;Q)\\u2245Q(\\u22121); also H_c^0(C)=0. Identifying M_{0,d+3} with the complement of the pairwise diagonals in B^d, set Mtilde:=C^d \\u00d7_{B^d} M_{0,d+3}. This is a nonempty Zariski-open in the irreducible d-fold C^d, hence irreducible, and Mtilde\\u2192M_{0,d+3} is connected finite etale. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places, for each of the d choices of factor, a direct summand Q(\\u22121)\\u2297(Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{\\u2297(d\\u22121)} inside Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(C^d;Q); the Hodge component (1,1)+(d\\u22121)\\u00b7(1,0)=(d,1) is one-dimensional and nonzero. The inverse image Y of the pairwise diagonals has dimension \\u2264d\\u22121, so the Hodge numbers of H_c^{d+1}(Y) vanish for p>dim Y and therefore F^d H_c^{d+1}(Y;C)=0. Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict for W and F; weights of H_c^d(Y;Q) are at most d; hence Gr^W_{d+1} of the compact-support localization sequence H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde)\\u2192H_c^{d+1}(C^d)\\u2192H_c^{d+1}(Y) is exact (FND-0165), the type-(d,1) class dies in H_c^{d+1}(Y), and it lifts to a nonzero class of Hodge type (d,1) in Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;Q). In particular F^d Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;C)\\u22600. For d\\u22652 one has d>(d+1)/2, so this weight-equals-degree corner is non-Tate. Now let W be a smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold equipped with a finite etale morphism f:W\\u2192M_{0,d+3}, and let W' be any connected component of W\\u00d7_{M_{0,d+3}} Mtilde. Then W'\\u2192W is finite etale of positive degree, W'\\u2192Mtilde is finite etale of positive degree, and finite-etale pullback/trace over Q injects the type-(d,1) class into Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(W';Q). The same non-Tate class is obtained if instead f is a dense open immersion, by a second application of FND-0165 to the complement of dimension \\u2264d\\u22121. Consequently the property that Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(\\u2212;Q) is Tate is not invariant under finite etale refinement of any such base, and no Tate assertion for that corner can be proved by an argument that is invariant under finite etale pullback, transfer, averaging, monodromy-orbit counting, or descent along an etale scheme atlas. This applies in particular to every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3. The statement does not apply to a merely dominant morphism that is neither finite etale nor an open immersion; it does not assert anything about compactly supported cohomology of a Deligne-Mumford stack in the absence of a scheme atlas; and it does not transport non-Tateness to Gr^W_{16} H_c^{16}(Z;Q) of a Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model, nor to RED-0001.`\\n\\n### `FND-0176` (L131)\\n`Work over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a geometric type-(i) fibre of H^bal in the sense of FND-0153, for instance any simply-branched balanced fibre (existence: FND-0172). Let B be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme. The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family over B with fibre (C_0,gamma_0) is an allowed ATT-0112 clause-(E) base, because its classifying image is a single type-(i) point. For this family, A=P_B(pi_*L) is isomorphic to B times |L_0| isomorphic to B times P^2, the reduced-support open U_0 of |L_0| is a nonempty smooth connected affine surface (the complement of the discriminant curve of the spanned g^2_6), U is isomorphic to B times U_0, and Z=Ord(U) isomorphic to B times Z_0 is the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. Poincare duality on the smooth connected surface U_0, equivalently compact-support localization of U_0 subset P^2 against the discriminant curve Delta_0 of dimension 1, yields H_c^4(U_0;Q) isomorphic to Q(-2), pure of type (2,2). Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures for products of separated finite-type C-schemes (the compact-support form of Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Proposition 8.2.10) therefore realises H_c^m(B;Q)(-2) as a direct mixed-Hodge-structure summand of H_c^{m+4}(U;Q) for every integer m, and, Q(-2) being pure of weight 4 with Gr^W exact, realises Gr^W_m H_c^m(B;Q)(-2) as a direct summand of Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(U;Q). Finite-etale transfer over Q identifies Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(U;Q) with the S_6-invariants inside Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(Z;Q). Consequently any theorem asserting that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8) for every allowed clause-(E) base forces Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(B;Q) to be a finite direct sum of Q(-6) for every reduced separated finite-type C-scheme B. This last assertion is false: if C is the affine Kummer curve of FND-0170 (the smooth projective model of y^3=x(x-1) minus the three ramification points of x), then for B=C^8 compact-support Kunneth supplies a nonzero Hodge component of type (8,4) in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(B;Q), namely Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{tensor 4} with the type-(1,0) line of H^1(Cbar) in each of the four H_c^1 factors, and tensoring with Q(-2) produces a nonzero type-(10,6) class in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) and hence in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q). Type (10,6) satisfies Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) for dim U=10 and is not of type (8,8), so Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and T_16(Z) is not a finite direct sum of Q(8). The exact C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem of campaign revision 4, universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus, is therefore false. A repaired C66-TATE-SUPPORT must either name a specific base or atlas, or retain the FND-0167 hypotheses (H-S) including the j=6 corner Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q). The exhibited class is the third FND-0167 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2), realised as a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself on a product family, not a lift of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S); FND-0171, which blocks transport of the j=8 first summand through the corner injection on a pure-dimension-15 atlas, does not apply. Not asserted: any computation of the global kernel K, any conclusion about a fixed 15-dimensional atlas of Hbar^bal, or any statement about RED-0001.`\\n\\n### `FND-0177` (L132)\\n`Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme, let Delta_0 subset P^2 be a closed subscheme of dimension at most 1, and set U_0=P^2 minus Delta_0. For a product (equivalently, constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL)) family with U isomorphic to S times U_0, compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures and the projective-bundle formula identify Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S times P^2;Q) with the direct sum of three pure weight-16 summands Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^{14}(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2), corresponding to fibre degrees 2j for j=0,1,2. Compact-support localization along U_0 subset P^2 is a long exact sequence of mixed Hodge structures; at the weight-equals-degree corner Gr^W is exact, so the fibre-degree-2j projective-bundle summand of A=S times P^2 lies in the image of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) if and only if the restriction Gr^W_{2j} H_c^{2j}(P^2;Q) -> Gr^W_{2j} H_c^{2j}(Delta_0;Q) vanishes. Vanishing of H_c^{2j}(Delta_0;Q) is sufficient for that restriction to vanish, and holds whenever 2j>2 dim Delta_0. Thus the fibre-degree-2 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) always survives in such product families as a direct Kunneth summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), equivalently H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2), because H_c^4 of a curve vanishes; this is the class used by ATT-0119. If Delta_0 is nonempty and proper then H_c^0(U_0;Q)=0, so the fibre-degree-0 summand Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) does not appear in H_c^{16}(U;Q); the restriction H_c^2(P^2)->H_c^2(Delta_0) is typically nonzero for a positive-degree plane curve, so the fibre-degree-1 projective-bundle summand need not arise from U. Independently, on a non-product FND-0167 family with S of pure dimension 15, the discriminant Delta subset A has dimension 16, so Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0. This is why FND-0171 blocks transporting the (H-S) j=8 / fibre-degree-0 first summand of ATT-0118 to U, while it does not block the ATT-0119 fibre-fundamental-class class, which is already a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself. The FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into the three summands and cannot by itself transport non-Tateness from any ambient summand to U; survival of the third summand in product families is a kernel/Kunneth statement, not a reverse of that injection. Fibrewise restriction on Delta_0 does not by itself control non-product families at fibre degrees j=0,1 without a compact-support Leray argument, which FND-0164 withholds for nonconstant coefficients. No assertion is made about RED-0001, about T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a dimension-15 atlas of Hbar^bal, or about S_6-isotypics other than the S_6-invariants of the product model.`\\n\\n### `FND-0178` (L133)\\n`Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let C_aff be the smooth connected affine curve obtained from the smooth projective model Cbar of y^3=x(x-1) by deleting the three ramification points of the degree-three x-map: Cbar has genus one by Riemann-Hurwitz, H_c^2(C_aff;Q)=Q(-1) of type (1,1), and Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q) is isomorphic to H^1(Cbar;Q) of types (1,0) and (0,1). Let S=C_aff^8, a smooth connected affine C-scheme of dimension 8, in particular reduced, locally Noetherian, separated, and of finite type. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places a nonzero Hodge type-(8,4) class in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q), arising from the summand Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q))^{tensor 4}. Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a simply-branched balanced type-(i) geometric fibre of H^bal (existence by FND-0172, equivalently Bujokas-Patel: the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of a general cover in H_{d,g} is balanced for g>=(d-3)(d-1), hence at (d,g)=(4,6)). The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL)