nsion d, and let Y be a closed finite-type subscheme or closed substack. Mixed Hodge structures on Borel-Moore homology are those of Deligne, and morphisms are strict for the weight filtration. For smooth X the lowest-weight piece W_{-k}H^{BM}_k(X;Q) is pure of weight -k: geometric Poincare duality identifies H^{BM}_k(X) with H_c^{2d-k}(X)(d), whose weights are at most -k, equivalently under the Hom convention H^{BM}_k:=Hom(H_c^k,Q) used by Canning-Larson-Payne. Purity of this piece, the numerical coincidence of Borel-Moore degree k with weight -k, and the mere existence of a closed support Y do not force the image of W_{-k}H^{BM}_k(Y;Q) -> W_{-k}H^{BM}_k(X;Q) to be a Tate Hodge structure. In particular, matching the C66-001 ledger (d,k)=(21,16): let A be a complex abelian variety of dimension 9, let X=A x P^{12} (smooth projective of dimension 21), and let Y=A x {pt} (closed embedding of codimension 12). Then H^*(A;Q) is the exterior algebra on H^1(A;Q) as Hodge structures, H^1(A) is pure of weight 1 with types (1,0) and (0,1) of dimension 9, and H^2(A) is therefore pure of weight 2 with types (2,0), (1,1), (0,2) and h^{2,0}=binomial(9,2)=36 nonzero. Kunneth together with the Gysin map of a point {pt} subset P^{12}, whose class generates H^{24}(P^{12};Q) isomorphic to Q(-12), realises H^2(A)(-12) as a direct summand of H^{26}(X;Q). Geometric Poincare duality with twist (21) identifies this summand with H^2(A)(9) inside W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(X;Q), and the Borel-Moore pushforward H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> H^{BM}_{16}(X;Q) is an isomorphism onto that summand. The Tate-twist convention V(m)^{p,q}=V^{p+m,q+m} (weight decreased by 2m) sends the types of H^2(A) to (-7,-9), (-8,-8), and (-9,-7) on H^2(A)(9), which is polarizable, pure of weight -16, and not a finite direct sum of Q(8). Consequently any argument for the C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem at (g,n)=(6,6), that the named kernel-form subobject T_Z=im(W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q)->T) of T:=W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(8), cannot conclude from purity, Borel-Moore degree 16, weight -16, and closed support in a smooth 21-fold alone. Additional geometric input is required, such as: (i) dim Y<=8, which forces W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) itself to vanish if dim Y<8 or to be a finite direct sum of Q(8) if Y has dimension 8 (top Borel-Moore); (ii) Tate type of the relevant lowest-weight groups on residual strata of dimensions 9 through 16; or (iii) vanishing of every non-Tate summand of W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) in the map to T. This statement does not assert that the named T_Z of M_{6,6} is non-Tate, does not refute RED-0001, and does not supply a Gysin computation on the Casnati-Ekedahl classifying-image closure.`\\n\\n### `FND-0195` (L166)\\n`Let g>=2, n>=1, and work with rational coefficients on Deligne-Mumford stacks. Write C^n for the n-fold fibre product of the closed universal curve pi:C->M_g, and set k=vcd(M_{g,n})=4g-4+n. The open immersion M_{g,n} subset C^n induces a surjection W_k H^k(C^n;Q) ->> W_k H^k(M_{g,n};Q) by Deligne's identification of the lowest-weight piece in degree k. Canning-Larson-Payne Lemma 3.1(a) then supplies an isomorphism of pure weight-k Hodge structures W_k H^k(M_{g,n};Q)/(Phi_{g,n}^k+Psi_{g,n}^k) congruent to the direct sum over |lambda|=n of W_k H^{k-n}(M_g;V_lambda) tensor V_{lambda^T}, where Phi_{g,n}^k=sum_i pi_i^* W_k H^k(M_{g,n-1};Q) and Psi_{g,n}^k=sum_i psi_i Phi_{g,n}^{k-2}; the identification of Psi with the Kunneth summands having some i_s=2, modulo Phi, is the published pi_2-projector statement of that lemma (Petersen-Tavakol-Yin), not a fibrewise canonical-class slogan. Harer's virtual cohomological dimension gives H^p(M_g;L)=0 for every Q-local system L and every p>vcd(M_g)=4g-5 (equivalently: cohomological dimension of a torsion-free finite-index subgroup, transferred by rational Hochschild-Serre). Hence every multi-index i in {0,1,2}^n with |i|<=n has base degree k-|i|>=4g-4>4g-5 and the primitive quotient vanishes. Independently