ultiplication by psi_s (or omega_s) spans the i_s=2 summands because the class restricts to a nonzero multiple of the fibre canonical class' must dispose of the slot-1 cross term b_s. Three disposals are valid over Q. (1) The slot-1 summand vanishes: H^1(M_g; R^1 pi_* Q) isomorphic to H^1(Mod_g; H^1(Sigma_g; Q))=0 for g>=2. This is the rational form of Morita's theorem H_1(Mod_g; H_1(Sigma_g; Z)) isomorphic to Z/(2g-2) for g>=2, recorded as H^1(Gamma_g, H_Q)=0 by Hain-Reed; equivalently H^2(C; Q) has basis {lambda, omega}, so the H^1(M_g; V) summand of H^2(C) is zero, hence b_s=0 identically and modulo slot-0 summands multiplication by omega_s coincides with multiplication by c_s. (2) The relative Chow-Kunneth projector of Petersen-Tavakol-Yin, pi_2 = psi_2/(2g-2) - kappa_1/(2(2g-2)^2), already lies in the Q-span of a psi class and a pullback from M_g, so it realises the i_s=0 to i_s=2 isomorphism inside Psi+Phi; Canning-Larson-Payne Lemma 3.1 invokes these projectors. (3) Downward induction on |i|: writing A_i for the multi-index summand of W_k H^k(C^n) and B_{i'} for the class with slot s reset to 0, one has A_i = c_s B_{i'} inside omega_s B_{i'} + A_{i'} + A_{i''} with |i''|=|i|-1, using the base case A_j=0 whenever k-|j| exceeds vcd(M_g)=4g-5. Disposal (3) applies in particular at the campaign point (g,n,k)=(6,6,26), where every multi-index with |i|<=6 has base degree at least 20>19. Thus the containment of i_s=2 summands in Phi+Psi holds over Q, but a fibre-restriction sentence does not by itself justify it.`\\n\\n### `FND-0197` (L168)\\n`Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let g>=2 and n>=2. Let pi:C->M_g be the universal closed curve of genus g, and let C^n be its n-fold fibre product over M_g, a smooth separated finite-type Deligne-Mumford stack. Identify M_{g,n} with the open complement in C^n of the union of pairwise diagonals. Then, for every integer k, restriction along this open immersion is a morphism of mixed Hodge structures inducing a surjection W_k H^